{
 "source": "fm-21-305",
 "leaf": 91,
 "label": "17-4",
 "width": 1992,
 "height": 3048,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "FM 21-305/AFMAN 24-306",
   "x": 88,
   "right": 574,
   "top": 39,
   "bottom": 77,
   "height": 38
  },
  {
   "text": "Operating Procedure",
   "x": 88,
   "right": 523,
   "top": 234,
   "bottom": 285,
   "height": 51
  },
  {
   "text": "To put the vehicle in motion -",
   "x": 85,
   "right": 588,
   "top": 322,
   "bottom": 374,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "e Apply the foot brake.",
   "x": 115,
   "right": 512,
   "top": 417,
   "bottom": 470,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "e Select the proper transmission lever position —",
   "x": 116,
   "right": 939,
   "top": 514,
   "bottom": 566,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "forward or reverse.",
   "x": 156,
   "right": 475,
   "top": 561,
   "bottom": 600,
   "height": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "e Place the transfer shift lever in the appropriate",
   "x": 116,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 654,
   "bottom": 707,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "range.",
   "x": 158,
   "right": 255,
   "top": 716,
   "bottom": 755,
   "height": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "e Check traffic conditions front and rear, using",
   "x": 118,
   "right": 947,
   "top": 798,
   "bottom": 853,
   "height": 55
  },
  {
   "text": "mirrors if necessary.",
   "x": 157,
   "right": 495,
   "top": 845,
   "bottom": 898,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "e Release the parking brake.",
   "x": 119,
   "right": 603,
   "top": 941,
   "bottom": 993,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "e Check again for traffic blind spots to the left or",
   "x": 119,
   "right": 946,
   "top": 1037,
   "bottom": 1090,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "right rear. Signal if pulling away from a curb.",
   "x": 157,
   "right": 915,
   "top": 1081,
   "bottom": 1142,
   "height": 61
  },
  {
   "text": "e Release the foot brake.",
   "x": 119,
   "right": 540,
   "top": 1181,
   "bottom": 1220,
   "height": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "e Depress the accelerator pedal gradually for a",
   "x": 120,
   "right": 945,
   "top": 1276,
   "bottom": 1329,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "smooth start.",
   "x": 158,
   "right": 373,
   "top": 1325,
   "bottom": 1363,
   "height": 38
  },
  {
   "text": "CAUTION",
   "x": 430,
   "right": 604,
   "top": 1469,
   "bottom": 1506,
   "height": 37
  },
  {
   "text": "Government vehicle operators are not per-",
   "x": 149,
   "right": 882,
   "top": 1563,
   "bottom": 1617,
   "height": 54
  },
  {
   "text": "mitted to tow or push automatic shift",
   "x": 148,
   "right": 883,
   "top": 1609,
   "bottom": 1662,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "vehicles for the purpose of starting them.",
   "x": 146,
   "right": 836,
   "top": 1657,
   "bottom": 1710,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "(For Air Force Only: During normal duty",
   "x": 146,
   "right": 883,
   "top": 1753,
   "bottom": 1806,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "hours, contact the maintenance control",
   "x": 146,
   "right": 881,
   "top": 1803,
   "bottom": 1848,
   "height": 45
  },
  {
   "text": "section of vehicle maintenance to start the",
   "x": 148,
   "right": 881,
   "top": 1850,
   "bottom": 1889,
   "height": 39
  },
  {
   "text": "vehicle with a booster battery, jumper",
   "x": 146,
   "right": 880,
   "top": 1898,
   "bottom": 1951,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "cables, or other equipment. After duty",
   "x": 148,
   "right": 883,
   "top": 1946,
   "bottom": 1999,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "hours, contact vehicle operations for",
   "x": 147,
   "right": 881,
   "top": 1992,
   "bottom": 2045,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "wrecker service. For detailed instructions,",
   "x": 146,
   "right": 880,
   "top": 2041,
   "bottom": 2086,
   "height": 45
  },
  {
   "text": "see your supervisor.)",
   "x": 147,
   "right": 506,
   "top": 2090,
   "bottom": 2142,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "JUMP STARTING VEHICLES",
   "x": 191,
   "right": 833,
   "top": 2225,
   "bottom": 2272,
   "height": 47
  },
  {
   "text": "Thousands of people are injured each year from",
   "x": 83,
   "right": 945,
   "top": 2331,
   "bottom": 2388,
   "height": 57
  },
  {
   "text": "auto battery explosions. Nearly two-thirds of these",
   "x": 84,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 2380,
   "bottom": 2433,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "injuries involve the eyes. Most soldiers, at one time",
   "x": 84,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 2428,
   "bottom": 2480,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "or another, will use jumper cables to start a vehicle,",
   "x": 85,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 2476,
   "bottom": 2528,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "and chances are they are not aware of the danger",
   "x": 84,
   "right": 944,
   "top": 2525,
   "bottom": 2578,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "involved. As a commander or supervisor, you are",
   "x": 84,
   "right": 942,
   "top": 2573,
   "bottom": 2625,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "responsible for the arall of your troops, both on and",
   "x": 84,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 2619,
   "bottom": 2705,
   "height": 86
  },
  {
   "text": "off duty. Stress that they should use one of the",
   "x": 85,
   "right": 943,
   "top": 2667,
   "bottom": 2720,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "procedures below to jump start a vehicle.",
   "x": 83,
   "right": 774,
   "top": 2714,
   "bottom": 2767,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "17-4",
   "x": 87,
   "right": 159,
   "top": 2910,
   "bottom": 2945,
   "height": 35
  },
  {
   "text": "Using Jumper Cables to Start Engine",
   "x": 1048,
   "right": 1819,
   "top": 232,
   "bottom": 283,
   "height": 51
  },
  {
   "text": "Use the following procedure to start an engine using",
   "x": 1046,
   "right": 1910,
   "top": 319,
   "bottom": 372,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "jumper cables on a 12-volt system (Figure 17-1):",
   "x": 1041,
   "right": 1853,
   "top": 369,
   "bottom": 421,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "e Position the jump starting vehicle with batteries",
   "x": 1078,
   "right": 1905,
   "top": 463,
   "bottom": 515,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "opposite the batteries of the disabled vehicle.",
   "x": 1118,
   "right": 1877,
   "top": 511,
   "bottom": 564,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "© Stop the engine of the jump starting vehicle.",
   "x": 1078,
   "right": 1856,
   "top": 605,
   "bottom": 658,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "e Open battery compartment doors of both",
   "x": 1079,
   "right": 1909,
   "top": 699,
   "bottom": 752,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "vehicles. Pull both battery boxes onto running",
   "x": 1116,
   "right": 1910,
   "top": 748,
   "bottom": 800,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "boards.",
   "x": 1117,
   "right": 1234,
   "top": 798,
   "bottom": 836,
   "height": 38
  },
  {
   "text": "WARNING",
   "x": 1380,
   "right": 1569,
   "top": 942,
   "bottom": 979,
   "height": 37
  },
  {
   "text": "One jumper cable must connect positive",
   "x": 1111,
   "right": 1845,
   "top": 1038,
   "bottom": 1090,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "terminals. The other jumper cable must",
   "x": 1110,
   "right": 1846,
   "top": 1085,
   "bottom": 1138,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "connect the negative terminal of the jum",
   "x": 1110,
   "right": 1821,
   "top": 1133,
   "bottom": 1186,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "starting vehicle to the body of the disabled",
   "x": 1110,
   "right": 1844,
   "top": 1180,
   "bottom": 1233,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "vehicle away from the batteries. Failure to",
   "x": 1108,
   "right": 1845,
   "top": 1228,
   "bottom": 1281,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "do so may cause batteries to explode, injur-",
   "x": 1111,
   "right": 1844,
   "top": 1277,
   "bottom": 1329,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "ing or killing personnel.",
   "x": 1110,
   "right": 1505,
   "top": 1324,
   "bottom": 1376,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "e Clamp one jumper cable (2) to the positive",
   "x": 1079,
   "right": 1907,
   "top": 1514,
   "bottom": 1566,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "terminal (1) of the ump starting vehicle and the",
   "x": 1118,
   "right": 1908,
   "top": 1562,
   "bottom": 1648,
   "height": 86
  },
  {
   "text": "positive terminal (3) of the disabled vehicle.",
   "x": 1117,
   "right": 1853,
   "top": 1610,
   "bottom": 1662,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "e Clamp the other jumper cable (5) to the nega-",
   "x": 1079,
   "right": 1908,
   "top": 1704,
   "bottom": 1756,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "tive terminal (6) of the jump starting vehicle and",
   "x": 1118,
   "right": 1909,
   "top": 1753,
   "bottom": 1806,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "the body (4) of the disabled vehicle.",
   "x": 1117,
   "right": 1717,
   "top": 1801,
   "bottom": 1854,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "e Start the engine of the jump starting vehicle.",
   "x": 1079,
   "right": 1859,
   "top": 1896,
   "bottom": 1949,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "e Start the engine of the disabled vehicle. If the",
   "x": 1079,
   "right": 1906,
   "top": 1991,
   "bottom": 2044,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "engine does not start after four tries, notify your",
   "x": 1117,
   "right": 1908,
   "top": 2039,
   "bottom": 2092,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "supervisor.",
   "x": 1118,
   "right": 1286,
   "top": 2091,
   "bottom": 2141,
   "height": 50
  },
  {
   "text": "WARNING",
   "x": 1378,
   "right": 1567,
   "top": 2232,
   "bottom": 2269,
   "height": 37
  },
  {
   "text": "Be sure jumper cable clamps do not con-",
   "x": 1107,
   "right": 1841,
   "top": 2325,
   "bottom": 2378,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "tact other jumper cable clamps or ter-",
   "x": 1108,
   "right": 1840,
   "top": 2375,
   "bottom": 2429,
   "height": 54
  },
  {
   "text": "ailure to do so may cause",
   "x": 1315,
   "right": 1842,
   "top": 2421,
   "bottom": 2474,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "minals.",
   "x": 1108,
   "right": 1239,
   "top": 2422,
   "bottom": 2460,
   "height": 38
  },
  {
   "text": "batteries to explode, injuring or killing",
   "x": 1105,
   "right": 1843,
   "top": 2471,
   "bottom": 2524,
   "height": 53
  },
  {
   "text": "personnel.",
   "x": 1106,
   "right": 1281,
   "top": 2521,
   "bottom": 2573,
   "height": 52
  },
  {
   "text": "@ Remove jumper cables (2) and (5).",
   "x": 1077,
   "right": 1698,
   "top": 2663,
   "bottom": 2715,
   "height": 52
  }
 ]
}
